{"t":"say","text":"I'll draw a small company website in Singapore with two ECS instances behind an ALB, plus RDS and OSS."}
{"t":"plan","products":["users","dns","alb","ecs","ess","rds","oss","sls"]}
{"t":"group","id":"internet","kind":"external","label":"Internet","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"users","product":"users","label":"Visitors","group":"internet","why":"People browsing the company website."}
{"t":"node","id":"dns","product":"dns","label":"Cloud DNS","group":null,"why":"Resolves the company domain to the ALB."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-dns","from":"users","to":"dns","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"group","id":"sg","kind":"region","label":"Singapore (ap-southeast-1)","parent":null}
{"t":"group","id":"vpc","kind":"vpc","label":"Website VPC","parent":"sg"}
{"t":"node","id":"alb","product":"alb","label":"ALB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Distributes visitor traffic across both ECS instances."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-alb","from":"users","to":"alb","label":"HTTPS"}
{"t":"node","id":"web","product":"ecs","label":"Web servers","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Two ECS instances hosting the company website."}
{"t":"node","id":"scaling","product":"ess","label":"Auto Scaling","group":"vpc","attachTo":"web","why":"Replaces unhealthy instances automatically."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-alb-web","from":"alb","to":"web"}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"RDS database","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Stores website content and user data with HA."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-web-db","from":"web","to":"db","label":"SQL"}
{"t":"node","id":"assets","product":"oss","label":"Static assets","group":"sg","why":"Holds images and files served by the website."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-web-assets","from":"web","to":"assets","label":"objects"}
{"t":"node","id":"logs","product":"sls","label":"Logs","group":"sg","why":"Collects web server access and error logs."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-web-logs","from":"web","to":"logs","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Small company website in Singapore with ALB, two ECS instances, RDS, OSS for assets and SLS for logs."}

{"t":"say","text":"Auto Scaling is already attached to your ECS instances. I'll add CloudMonitor so it can trigger scaling by CPU or request metrics."}
{"t":"req","text":"Servers scale out and in automatically based on weekend load"}
{"t":"node","id":"monitor","product":"cloudmonitor","label":"CloudMonitor","group":"sg","why":"Provides CPU and request metrics that drive Auto Scaling rules."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-web-monitor","from":"web","to":"monitor","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Added CloudMonitor to feed scaling metrics; Auto Scaling on the ECS instances will now scale out and in automatically on weekends."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll draw a serverless ticketing API on SAE behind an ALB with WAF, Tair cache and RDS database."}
{"t":"req","text":"Zero ops engineers: fully managed serverless stack preferred"}
{"t":"plan","products":["users","dns","alb","waf","sae","tair","rds","sls","cloudmonitor"]}
{"t":"group","id":"internet","kind":"external","label":"Internet","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"users","product":"users","label":"Ticket buyers & apps","group":"internet","why":"Clients calling the ticketing API."}
{"t":"node","id":"dns","product":"dns","label":"Cloud DNS","group":null,"why":"Resolves the API domain to the ALB."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-dns","from":"users","to":"dns","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"group","id":"sg","kind":"region","label":"Singapore (ap-southeast-1)","parent":null}
{"t":"group","id":"vpc","kind":"vpc","label":"Ticketing VPC","parent":"sg"}
{"t":"node","id":"alb","product":"alb","label":"ALB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Layer-7 ingress for the API across two zones."}
{"t":"node","id":"waf","product":"waf","label":"WAF","group":"vpc","attachTo":"alb","why":"Blocks bots and scalper attacks on ticket sales."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-alb","from":"users","to":"alb","label":"HTTPS"}
{"t":"node","id":"api","product":"sae","label":"Ticketing API","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Serverless app engine: no servers or ops to manage."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-alb-api","from":"alb","to":"api","label":"HTTP"}
{"t":"node","id":"cache","product":"tair","label":"Seat cache","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Caches seat availability for fast reads under load."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-api-cache","from":"api","to":"cache","label":"Redis"}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"Orders DB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Relational store for tickets, orders and payments."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-api-db","from":"api","to":"db","label":"SQL"}
{"t":"node","id":"logs","product":"sls","label":"Logs","group":"sg","why":"Centralized logs without running a logging stack."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-api-logs","from":"api","to":"logs","kind":"control"}
{"t":"node","id":"metrics","product":"cloudmonitor","label":"CloudMonitor","group":"sg","why":"Built-in metrics and alarms, zero ops overhead."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-api-metrics","from":"api","to":"metrics","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Serverless concert ticketing API on SAE behind ALB with WAF, Tair cache and RDS, plus SLS and CloudMonitor."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll add Auto Scaling to SAE for the traffic spike and recommend NAT Gateway so instances scale out freely."}
{"t":"req","text":"Must auto-scale for 20x traffic spike tomorrow"}
{"t":"node","id":"scaling","product":"ess","label":"Auto Scaling","group":"vpc","attachTo":"api","why":"Scales SAE pods automatically for 20x concert traffic spike."}
{"t":"rec","product":"nat","fit":"complement","why":"Gives scaled SAE pods outbound internet without manual EIP management."}
{"t":"rec","product":"pts","fit":"complement","why":"Load-test the ticketing API today to validate scaling before sales open."}
{"t":"done","summary":"Added Auto Scaling attached to SAE to handle 20x traffic spike; recommended NAT Gateway and load testing."}

{"t":"say","text":"For a team collaborating daily, Qoder Teams with a Token Plan gives shared seats and per-member API keys."}
{"t":"rec","product":"qoder-teams","fit":"primary","why":"Qoder seats for your engineering team with SSO, admin controls and usage analytics."}
{"t":"rec","product":"token-plan","fit":"complement","why":"Credit subscription providing per-member keys for the team's interactive coding tools."}
{"t":"rec","product":"qwenwork","fit":"complement","why":"Workplace agent for docs, slides and sheets that complements the coding workflow."}
{"t":"rec","product":"dingtalk","fit":"complement","why":"Team messaging that links to QwenWork for daily collaboration."}
{"t":"done","summary":"Recommended Qoder Teams as the primary plan with Token Plan for keys, plus QwenWork and DingTalk for collaboration."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll design a patient appointment booking app hosted in Seoul so health records never leave Korea."}
{"t":"req","text":"All health records must stay in South Korea (Seoul region)."}
{"t":"plan","products":["users","dns","esa","alb","waf","ecs","ess","tair","rds","oss","sls"]}
{"t":"group","id":"internet","kind":"external","label":"Internet","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"users","product":"users","label":"Patients and clinic staff","group":"internet","why":"People booking or managing appointments."}
{"t":"node","id":"dns","product":"dns","label":"Cloud DNS","group":null,"why":"Resolves the clinic domain to ESA."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-dns","from":"users","to":"dns","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"group","id":"edge","kind":"edge","label":"Edge","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"esa","product":"esa","label":"ESA","group":"edge","why":"Accelerates static assets and protects the site globally."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-esa","from":"users","to":"esa","label":"HTTPS"}
{"t":"group","id":"kr","kind":"region","label":"Seoul (ap-northeast-2)","parent":null}
{"t":"group","id":"vpc","kind":"vpc","label":"Clinic VPC","parent":"kr"}
{"t":"node","id":"alb","product":"alb","label":"ALB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Routes HTTPS traffic to web servers across two zones."}
{"t":"node","id":"waf","product":"waf","label":"WAF","group":"vpc","attachTo":"alb","why":"Blocks OWASP attacks on the booking portal."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-esa-alb","from":"esa","to":"alb","label":"origin"}
{"t":"node","id":"app","product":"ecs","label":"Booking web servers","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Runs the appointment booking application in two zones."}
{"t":"node","id":"scaling","product":"ess","label":"Auto Scaling","group":"vpc","attachTo":"app","why":"Scales servers during peak booking hours."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-alb-app","from":"alb","to":"app"}
{"t":"say","text":"Sessions go to Tair and appointments to RDS, both with zone redundancy."}
{"t":"node","id":"cache","product":"tair","label":"Session cache","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Stores user sessions for fast access."}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"Appointments DB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Stores patient and appointment data locally in Seoul."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-app-cache","from":"app","to":"cache"}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-app-db","from":"app","to":"db","label":"SQL"}
{"t":"node","id":"media","product":"oss","label":"Clinic assets","group":"kr","why":"Stores static files like logos and consent forms."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-esa-media","from":"esa","to":"media","label":"static"}
{"t":"node","id":"logs","product":"sls","label":"Logs","group":"kr","why":"Collects application logs within Korea for compliance."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-app-logs","from":"app","to":"logs","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Two-zone appointment booking app in Seoul behind ESA, ALB with WAF, ECS with Auto Scaling, Tair and RDS."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll add a cross-zone standby RDS, Cloud Backup for disaster recovery, and CloudMonitor for alerts."}
{"t":"req","text":"System must stay up if something fails (disaster recovery)."}
{"t":"plan","products":["cloud-backup","cloudmonitor"]}
{"t":"node","id":"backup","product":"cloud-backup","label":"Cloud Backup","group":"kr","why":"Backs up RDS and OSS for disaster recovery."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-db-backup","from":"db","to":"backup","kind":"control"}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-media-backup","from":"media","to":"backup","kind":"control"}
{"t":"node","id":"monitor","product":"cloudmonitor","label":"CloudMonitor","group":"kr","why":"Monitors resources and triggers failover alerts."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-app-monitor","from":"app","to":"monitor","kind":"control"}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-db-monitor","from":"db","to":"monitor","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Added Cloud Backup for DR and CloudMonitor for alerting; all data stays in Seoul region."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll add a dedicated OSS bucket for medical scans, kept in Seoul to meet data residency rules."}
{"t":"node","id":"scans","product":"oss","label":"Medical scans (MRI/CT)","group":"kr","why":"Stores uploaded MRI and CT scan files within Korea."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-app-scans","from":"app","to":"scans","label":"upload"}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-scans-backup","from":"scans","to":"backup","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Added a dedicated OSS bucket for medical scans with backup, all staying in Seoul."}

{"t":"say","text":"OpenSearch 노드를 Elasticsearch로 교체하겠습니다."}
{"t":"node","id":"search","product":"elasticsearch","label":"Product search","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"상품 검색을 위한 Elasticsearch 클러스터, 두 존에 배포하여 고가용성 확보."}
{"t":"done","summary":"상품 검색 엔진을 OpenSearch에서 Elasticsearch(2존)로 변경했습니다."}

{"t":"say","text":"已将订单消息队列从 RocketMQ 替换为 Kafka。"}
{"t":"node","id":"queue","product":"kafka","label":"Order events","group":"vpc","why":"Kafka 处理订单事件流，支持高吞吐和持久化。"}
{"t":"done","summary":"将订单消息队列从 RocketMQ 替换为 ApsaraMQ for Kafka，其余架构不变。"}

{"t":"req","text":"Monthly cloud budget max $150"}
{"t":"say","text":"I'll design a minimal blog using Simple Application Server, which bundles compute, disk and bandwidth in one plan."}
{"t":"plan","products":["users","dns","swas","oss","cdn"]}
{"t":"group","id":"internet","kind":"external","label":"Internet","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"users","product":"users","label":"Readers","group":"internet","why":"Visitors reading the newspaper blog."}
{"t":"node","id":"dns","product":"dns","label":"Alibaba Cloud DNS","group":null,"why":"Resolves the blog domain to the server IP."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-dns","from":"users","to":"dns","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"group","id":"sg","kind":"region","label":"Singapore (ap-southeast-1)","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"blog","product":"swas","label":"Blog server","group":"sg","why":"Runs the blog CMS on a low-cost bundled plan."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-blog","from":"users","to":"blog","label":"HTTPS"}
{"t":"node","id":"media","product":"oss","label":"Media storage","group":"sg","why":"Stores article images cheaply off the server."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-blog-media","from":"blog","to":"media","label":"upload"}
{"t":"group","id":"edge","kind":"edge","label":"Edge","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"cdn","product":"cdn","label":"CDN","group":"edge","why":"Caches images at the edge to cut OSS costs."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-cdn-media","from":"cdn","to":"media","label":"origin pull"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Budget blog on Simple Application Server with DNS, OSS for media and CDN caching."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll add an RDS MySQL database for comments. The blog server will read and write comment data directly."}
{"t":"plan","products":["rds"]}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"Comments DB","group":"sg","why":"Stores reader comments with managed backups and HA."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-blog-db","from":"blog","to":"db","label":"SQL"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Added RDS MySQL for the comment system, connected from the blog server."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll add a standby RDS instance for database resilience and use GTM with DNS to fail over if the blog goes down."}
{"t":"plan","products":["gtm"]}
{"t":"node","id":"gtm","product":"gtm","label":"GTM","group":null,"why":"Health-checks the blog and fails over DNS if it goes down."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-users-gtm","from":"users","to":"gtm","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"remove","id":"e-users-dns"}
{"t":"move","id":"db","to":"sg"}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"Comments DB (HA)","group":"sg","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Multi-zone RDS provides automatic failover for the comments database."}
{"t":"say","text":"For full blog HA on a $150 budget, consider adding a second SWAS in another zone behind a lightweight NLB."}
{"t":"done","summary":"Added GTM for DNS failover and upgraded RDS to multi-zone HA for database resilience within budget."}

{"t":"say","text":"For 12 developers using Cline in VS Code, Qoder Teams with a Coding Plan gives per-member fixed-cost keys."}
{"t":"rec","product":"qoder-teams","fit":"primary","why":"Seats for 12 devs with admin, SSO and usage analytics for Cline in VS Code."}
{"t":"rec","product":"coding-plan","fit":"complement","why":"Fixed-fee subscription providing per-member API keys for Cline, predictable monthly cost."}

{"t":"say","text":"Mumbai (ap-south-1) is closed. I'll use Singapore (ap-southeast-1), the nearest open region, with GA to lower latency for Indian players."}
{"t":"req","text":"Game servers in Mumbai; lowest latency for Indian players"}
{"t":"plan","products":["mobile-app","dns","ga","nlb","ecs","ess","tair","rds","sls","cloudmonitor"]}
{"t":"group","id":"internet","kind":"external","label":"Internet","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"players","product":"mobile-app","label":"Indian players","group":"internet","why":"Mobile gamers connecting from India."}
{"t":"node","id":"dns","product":"dns","label":"Alibaba Cloud DNS","group":null,"why":"Resolves game domain to Global Accelerator anycast IP."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-players-dns","from":"players","to":"dns","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"group","id":"edge","kind":"edge","label":"Edge","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"ga","product":"ga","label":"Global Accelerator","group":"edge","why":"Anycast entry near India, backbone to Singapore for low latency."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-players-ga","from":"players","to":"ga","label":"UDP/TCP"}
{"t":"group","id":"sg","kind":"region","label":"Singapore (ap-southeast-1)","parent":null}
{"t":"group","id":"vpc","kind":"vpc","label":"Game VPC","parent":"sg"}
{"t":"node","id":"nlb","product":"nlb","label":"NLB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Layer-4 load balancer for game traffic across zones."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-ga-nlb","from":"ga","to":"nlb","label":"backbone"}
{"t":"node","id":"gameserver","product":"ecs","label":"Game servers","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Runs multiplayer game sessions in two zones."}
{"t":"node","id":"scaling","product":"ess","label":"Auto Scaling","group":"vpc","attachTo":"gameserver","why":"Scales game servers with player count."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-nlb-gameserver","from":"nlb","to":"gameserver","label":"game"}
{"t":"node","id":"cache","product":"tair","label":"Session cache","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Stores player sessions and matchmaking state."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-gameserver-cache","from":"gameserver","to":"cache","label":"Redis"}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"Player DB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Persists player profiles, inventory and scores."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-gameserver-db","from":"gameserver","to":"db","label":"SQL"}
{"t":"node","id":"logs","product":"sls","label":"Logs","group":"sg","why":"Central game logs for debugging and analytics."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-gameserver-logs","from":"gameserver","to":"logs","kind":"control"}
{"t":"node","id":"monitor","product":"cloudmonitor","label":"CloudMonitor","group":"sg","why":"Alerts on server health and latency metrics."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-gameserver-monitor","from":"gameserver","to":"monitor","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"Multiplayer game architecture using Global Accelerator from India to Singapore, NLB, ECS game servers, Tair cache and RDS."}

{"t":"say","text":"I'll design a DDoS-hardened login API path: Anti-DDoS Proxy, ESA with WAF, NLB for TCP, and ECS backend."}
{"t":"plan","products":["users","dns","anti-ddos-proxy","esa","waf","nlb","ecs","ess","tair","rds","sls","cloudmonitor"]}
{"t":"group","id":"internet","kind":"external","label":"Internet","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"players","product":"users","label":"Game players","group":"internet","why":"Players calling the login API from game clients."}
{"t":"node","id":"dns","product":"dns","label":"Cloud DNS","group":null,"why":"Resolves the login domain to Anti-DDoS Proxy."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-players-dns","from":"players","to":"dns","kind":"resolve"}
{"t":"group","id":"edge","kind":"edge","label":"Edge protection","parent":null}
{"t":"node","id":"antiddos","product":"anti-ddos-proxy","label":"Anti-DDoS Proxy","group":"edge","why":"Scrubbing center absorbs massive L3-L7 DDoS floods before they reach origin."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-players-antiddos","from":"players","to":"antiddos","label":"HTTPS"}
{"t":"node","id":"esa","product":"esa","label":"ESA","group":"edge","why":"Edge acceleration plus bot management for the login API."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-antiddos-esa","from":"antiddos","to":"esa","label":"scrubbed"}
{"t":"group","id":"sg","kind":"region","label":"Singapore (ap-southeast-1)","parent":null}
{"t":"group","id":"vpc","kind":"vpc","label":"Game VPC","parent":"sg"}
{"t":"node","id":"nlb","product":"nlb","label":"NLB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Layer-4 load balancer handles high connection rates for login traffic."}
{"t":"node","id":"waf","product":"waf","label":"WAF 3.0","group":"vpc","attachTo":"nlb","why":"Blocks OWASP attacks and CC floods on the login endpoint."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-esa-nlb","from":"esa","to":"nlb","label":"origin"}
{"t":"node","id":"login","product":"ecs","label":"Login servers","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Runs the authentication service across two zones for HA."}
{"t":"node","id":"scaling","product":"ess","label":"Auto Scaling","group":"vpc","attachTo":"login","why":"Adds instances when attack traffic spikes or load rises."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-nlb-login","from":"nlb","to":"login","label":"TCP"}
{"t":"say","text":"Sessions go to Tair, credentials to RDS, both multi-zone for resilience."}
{"t":"node","id":"cache","product":"tair","label":"Session cache","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Stores login tokens and rate-limit counters in memory."}
{"t":"node","id":"db","product":"rds","label":"Accounts DB","group":"vpc","zones":["a","b"],"why":"Persists player credentials with zone-level failover."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-login-cache","from":"login","to":"cache","label":"sessions"}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-login-db","from":"login","to":"db","label":"SQL"}
{"t":"say","text":"Adding observability to detect attacks early and keep metrics flowing."}
{"t":"node","id":"logs","product":"sls","label":"Logs","group":"sg","why":"Centralizes access logs for forensic analysis during attacks."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-login-logs","from":"login","to":"logs","kind":"control"}
{"t":"node","id":"metrics","product":"cloudmonitor","label":"CloudMonitor","group":"sg","why":"Alarms on traffic spikes, CPU and error rates."}
{"t":"edge","id":"e-nlb-metrics","from":"nlb","to":"metrics","kind":"control"}
{"t":"done","summary":"DDoS-protected login API with Anti-DDoS Proxy, ESA, WAF on NLB, dual-zone ECS with Auto Scaling, Tair and RDS."}

